{"name":"Fern Gully","hex":"#595646","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fern Gully","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Singleton council area, eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fern_Gully"}],"entries":[{"title":"FernGully: The Last Rainforest","blocks":[{"text":"FernGully: The Last Rainforest is a 1992 animated musical fantasy film directed by Bill Kroyer from a screenplay by Jim Cox, based on the FernGully stories by Diana Young. It stars the voices of Samantha Mathis, Jonathan Ward, Tim Curry, Robin Williams, Christian Slater, and Grace Zabriskie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/Ferngully.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FernGully%3A_The_Last_Rainforest"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"},{"title":"Gully","blocks":[{"text":"A gully is a landform created by running water, mass movement, or both, which erodes soil to a sharp angle, typically on a hillside or in river floodplains or terraces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Vo%C3%A7oroca_%2823_12_24S_-_48_47_59W%29_-_REFON_3.JPG/330px-Vo%C3%